        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.252,
            0.079,
            0.823,
            0.101
          ],
          "content": "3. Fill in the blanks using the most appropriate option—"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.102,
            0.881,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": "(i) A fuel that is commonly used in two wheelers like scooters or bikes is......... (a) Kerosene (b) Petrol (c) Diesel (d) LPG"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.238,
            0.819,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "(ii) An example of a renewable resource is ......... (a) Coal (b) Water (c) Natural gas (d) Petrol"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.362,
            0.882,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": "4. Classify the following as renewable or non-renewable resources—coal, natural gas, forests and minerals."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.408,
            0.882,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "5. Why do we say that petroleum is a non-renewable resource?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.252,
            0.438,
            0.809,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": "6. It is difficult to regrow forests. Justify this statement."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.468,
            0.882,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": "7. Make a list of five daily activities in which you use natural resources. Suggest ways by which you can reduce their use."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.515,
            0.837,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "8. List four activities that are possible due to the presence of air."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.563,
            0.843,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": "9. How can you contribute towards enhancing the green cover of your locality? Make a list of actions to be taken."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.613,
            0.719,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": "10. In the given illustration, we see that food is being cooked."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.655,
            0.63,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": "Answer the following questions—"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.302,
            0.678,
            0.63,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": "(i) What type of energy is being used for cooking?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.302,
            0.72,
            0.545,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Name one benefit and one drawback of using this type of energy for cooking."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.802,
            0.6,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": "11. Cutting down trees on a large scale impacts the quality of the soil. Why do you think it is so?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.592,
            0.615,
            0.906,
            0.835
          ],
